<figure class="incident-figure" aria-labelledby="incident-space-title">
  <figcaption id="incident-space-title"><span class="figure-number">Figure 3</span> The repair needs space too</figcaption>
  <div class="incident-scene space-scene">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 330 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="space-title space-desc">
      <title id="space-title">Free space falls from 12 to 4 GiB in ten minutes</title>
      <desc id="space-desc">Synthetic observations at minute zero, five and ten show 12, 8 and 4 GiB free. A dashed line at 6 GiB shows the extra space assumed necessary for a proposed repair. The trajectory crosses it before minute ten. It is not safe to assume the repair fits just because some space remains.</desc>
      <g class="space-axis"><path d="M44 35V215H309" /><path d="M44 35H309 M44 95H309 M44 155H309" class="space-grid" /></g>
      <g class="space-label"><text x="6" y="40">12</text><text x="14" y="100">8</text><text x="14" y="160">4</text><text x="14" y="220">0</text><text x="44" y="245">0</text><text x="171" y="245">5</text><text x="291" y="245">10</text><text x="44" y="19">GiB free</text><text x="213" y="245">minutes</text></g>
      <path class="space-repair" d="M44 125H309" />
      <text class="space-label" x="65" y="148">Repair: 6 GiB extra</text>
      <path class="space-line" d="M44 35L175 95L306 155" />
      <g class="space-points"><circle cx="44" cy="35" r="5" /><circle cx="175" cy="95" r="5" /><circle cx="306" cy="155" r="5" /></g>
    </svg>
    <p class="figure-explanation">At minute 10, 4 GiB remains. A repair needing 6 GiB of extra peak space already does not fit.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="incident-caption">Invented free-space observations on one volume. The 6 GiB requirement is an assumed repair estimate, not a database threshold. At the same net growth rate the remaining 4 GiB would last five more minutes; the workload and the rate can change.</p>
</figure>
